# S18 checkpoint vs. the console's claim target - 2026-09-13
#
# The human authorised adding 'claim' to the allowlist once the page needed it: console/serve.py's
# GET /claim runs `make -s claim NS=... MODULE=...`, and the Makefile had no such target. This
# records the frozen file's failure with 12 expected names against a Makefile that prints 13, then
# the same file's PASS with only that one name added - the assertion code unchanged.
#
# The frozen file was never edited while it was failing. `git hash-object scripts/checks/S18.sh` and
# `git rev-parse HEAD:scripts/checks/S18.sh` were both e4d858c3feee2bccffd064814b6b3394dfdc1bf3
# before the runs and after them. The copy the second run used is shown below - one line - and it was
# deleted once the run finished, so scripts/checks/ holds the frozen file alone.

--- BEFORE: scripts/checks/S18.sh as frozen, Makefile printing 13 names (2026-09-13 02:13:41)

