--- Why this PASS is evidence, and an earlier one was not
#
# The checkpoint's last two assertions read the cluster, and a read of an empty cluster satisfies
# them vacuously. The run above is the second attempt. The first (02:13:41-02:15:52) is DISCARDED: at
# 01:15:11Z a `make destroy` started from the console's own destroy button took the whole stack down
# while that run was asleep, so its last two ok lines were computed against zero claims. That is what
# docs/evidence/state.log shows for it, the final reads being
# `up=false running=0 claims=` at 01:15:18Z and 01:15:20Z.
#
# The stack was then rebuilt with `make demo-up` and the run above made these reads (same log):
#
#   2026-09-13T01:25:27Z up=true  running=3  claims=pgadmin:Ready,postgres:Ready,redis:Ready
#   2026-09-13T01:25:28Z up=false running=0  claims=      <- assertion 5, the deliberate no-cluster read
#   2026-09-13T01:26:22Z up=true  running=3  claims=pgadmin:Orphaned,postgres:Orphaned,redis:Ready
#   2026-09-13T01:26:57Z up=true  running=3  claims=pgadmin:Ready,postgres:Ready,redis:Ready
#
# The Orphaned read is assertion 8's first half with real data; the all-Ready read is its second half,
# and it is the read the two disputed assertions were computed from. `docker ps` showed 3/3 containers
# afterwards, and docs/evidence/{destroy,console-destroy}.log mtimes were unchanged (02:15:11).

--- One thing the rebuild exposed, recorded as an observation
#
# That `make demo-up` exited 2: the app's own R-checks were `12 PASS, 5 FAIL`, and all five are the
# Ingress-facing checks - R1, R2, R5, R6, R8, every one reporting curl `code=000`, no connection.
# R13 and R16 use the identical `curl -sk --compressed` against the same https://vote.localhost:8082
# and PASSED later in the same run, and the probe before the checkpoint returned `vote=200
# result=200`, so the endpoint became reachable while verify was running. That is the observation;
# the cause is not established here, and it is not one of this checkpoint's assertions. It is
# independent of the allowlist change, which adds a target and a name and touches no HTTP path.
